## Getting started

```bash
go mod tidy
go run ./{{if eq .Arch "simple"}}.{{else}}cmd/server{{end}}
```

## Configuration

Settings live in [`configs/config.yaml`](configs/config.yaml) and are loaded with
[Viper](https://github.com/spf13/viper). Any value can be overridden by an
environment variable — e.g. `SERVER_PORT`{{if ne .Arch "simple"}}, `DATABASE_URL` (see `.env.example`){{end}}.

The API is served under `/api/v1`.{{if eq .Arch "microservice"}} Health: `GET /healthz`. gRPC listens on `:9090`.{{end}}

## Layout

{{if eq .Arch "simple"}}Flat single-package app; one file per entity with an in-memory store.{{else if eq .Arch "layered"}}Classic layered app: `internal/{model,repository,service,handler}`.{{else if eq .Arch "clean"}}Clean architecture: `internal/{domain,application,infrastructure,interface}`.{{else if eq .Arch "microservice"}}Clean architecture plus gRPC, health checks, graceful shutdown and docker-compose.{{else if eq .Arch "monolith"}}Modular monolith: one bounded context per entity under `internal/<entity>/`.{{end}}
